{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song, a psalm of the sons of Korah</b> — Because מָחֲלַת opens לְעַד־נֶאֱמָן, which is in construct state, therefore I said that this song concerns the pleasantness of the piyyut; at the beginning of the piyyut [the word] מחלת was attached to it, whether 'my heart' or 'my body' [follows it in the piyyut]. Also this psalm concerns the illness of the singer." "<b>And the word לַעֲנוֹת</b> — like קוֹל עָנוֹת. Rabbi Yeshuah said: this Heman is the grandson of Samuel, and Scripture calls him אָזְרָחִי because he is a native among singers, for most of the singers are his sons and grandsons, as written in Chronicles. And some say: that an alef is added, and he is a son of Zerah, and his brother is Ethan. And others said: that Heman and Ethan are brothers, and the name of their father was Azarch."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 88, :notes {1 "Resolved הימן as 'Heman' (1 Chronicles 6:18ff.) and retained אזרחי / אזרח in transliterated form since Ibn Ezra plays on the root אזרח across all three interpretations."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:18.877028801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}